@roidelapluie Thanks for reaching out, the method you mentioned `NewVirtualMachinesClientWithBaseURI` is an old way of using SDK, that requires you provide a resource endpoint to tell SDK what is the current Azure cloud you are working with, in our new SDK, this is can be achieved by the below code
```golang
import {
   "github.com/Azure/azure-sdk-for-go/sdk/resourcemanager/compute/armcompute"
}

options := arm.ClientOptions {
    ClientOptions: azcore.ClientOptions {
        Cloud: cloud.AzureChina,
    },
}
client, err := armcompute.NewVirtualMachinesClient("subscriptionid", cred, &options)
```
By using the above code, you don't need to specify the resource endpoint every time when you are creating new resource client

You can refer to this sample for more details of how to operate azure resource using our new sdk: [Create VM using new Azure SDK for golang](https://github.com/Azure-Samples/azure-sdk-for-go-samples/blob/main/sdk/resourcemanager/compute/create_vm/main.go)
